# Line-ending policy: LF everywhere, on every OS.
#
# Pinning `eol=lf` (not just `text=auto`) is deliberate: with core.autocrlf=true
# on Windows, a bare `text=auto` lets git rewrite the working tree to CRLF while
# the repo blobs and our formatters (biome --write, prettier, etc.) emit LF. That
# mismatch flags untouched files as "modified" (LF<->CRLF) whenever any tool
# rewrites them. eol=lf makes the working-tree ending deterministic and stops it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Scripts that are sensitive to their line endings.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf

# Known binary formats — never normalize or diff as text.
*.sl2  binary
*.dat  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
